'''性交疼痛'''（{{langx|en|Dyspareunia}}<ref name="SurgeryInAlleviationOfDysparenuia">{{Cite journal |last=Agnew |first=A. M. |date=1959-06-13 |title=Surgery in the Alleviation of Dyspareunia |url=https://www.bmj.com/lookup/doi/10.1136/bmj.1.5136.1510 |journal=BMJ |language=en |volume=1 |issue=5136 |doi=10.1136/bmj.1.5136.1510 |issn=0959-8138 |pmc=1993727 |pmid=13651780}}</ref>），是指经常或反复于性交时出现的[[外阴]]、[[阴道]]或[[下腹]]部[[疼痛]]为主要症状的疾病，也称'''性生活不适'''，是[[女性性功能障碍]]中最常见的一种。它包括性交痛以及由此而导致的[[性交不能]]。前者仅表现为每于性交时阴道、外阴或下腹部疼痛，后者由于疼痛严重，致使[[阴茎]]不被允许或无法进入前庭及插入[[阴道]]，使[[性交]]过程无法进行。它可能是由心理原因或生理原因导致，并常见于女性<ref name="Schein1988">{{Cite journal |last=Schein |first=M. |last2=Zyzanski |first2=S. J. |last3=Levine |first3=S. |last4=Medalie |first4=J. H. |last5=Dickman |first5=R. L. |last6=Alemagno |first6=S. A. |date=1988 |title=The frequency of sexual problems among family practice patients |url=https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3274680/ |journal=Family Practice Research Journal |volume=7 |issue=3 |issn=0270-2304 |pmid=3274680 |access-date=2022-11-17 |archive-date=2022-11-17 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221117150635/https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3274680/ |dead-url=no }}</ref>。

对于性交疼痛的医疗评估常常先考虑生理原因多于心理原因。在大多数性交疼痛病例中，均有生理原因存在。对于女性{{le|骨盆底|pelvic floor}}肌肉产生的不自觉肌肉收缩病症称之为[[阴道痉挛]]。根据《[[精神病诊断与统计手册]]》（第四版）<ref>{{cite book|title=Diagnostic and statistical manual of mental disorders: DSM-IV|publisher=American Psychiatric Association|location=Washington, DC|year=1994|isbn=0-89042-062-9|edition=4th|author=the American Psychiatric Association.}}</ref>，性交疼痛通常发生于性交过程前、中间、后所有持续性、复发性疼痛，这些并非仅仅是缺乏[[阴道润滑]]或阴道痉挛。现有文献就引起性交疼痛的原因存在分歧<ref name="binik2005">{{Cite journal |last=Binik |first=Yitzchak M. |date=2005-02 |title=Should Dyspareunia Be Retained as a Sexual Dysfunction in DSM-V? A Painful Classification Decision |url=http://link.springer.com/10.1007/s10508-005-0998-4 |journal=Archives of Sexual Behavior |language=en |volume=34 |issue=1 |doi=10.1007/s10508-005-0998-4 |issn=0004-0002 |pmid=15772767}}</ref><ref name="moser2005">{{Cite journal |last=Moser |first=Charles |date=2005-02 |title=Dyspareunia: Another Argument for Removal |url=http://link.springer.com/10.1007/s10508-005-7473-z |journal=Archives of Sexual Behavior |language=en |volume=34 |issue=1 |doi=10.1007/s10508-005-7473-z |issn=0004-0002 |pmid=16092029}}</ref>。

